WEBVTT

00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:14,060
Why is iodine not a good idea for someone with breast cancer?

00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:16,940
I do not have a thyroid cancer.

00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:22,780
I take compounded thyroid medication and told there's a link between thyroid cancer and breast cancer.

00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:31,090
Well iodine can be a good thing for breast cancer used acutely.

00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:35,650
So I don't think that breast cancer patients should be on iodine or in turn.

00:00:35,810 --> 00:00:44,610
The problem with iodine or the thyroid is the thyroid needs iodine in order to make T3s.

00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:48,050
So that's a necessary component.

00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:54,850
But when we take exogenous iodine in a supplement, it's basically taking a hyperdose of iodine.

00:00:55,490 --> 00:01:02,530
You're really stimulating a lot of attraction to the thyroid gland by the immune system.

00:01:03,090 --> 00:01:10,530
And the chance of you developing an auto immune thyroid if you're taking iodine long term,

00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:16,050
the chance if you're developing a Hashimoto or Graves disease is almost 100%.

00:01:16,690 --> 00:01:19,970
That's why I'm not a fan of taking iodine long term.

00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:24,770
So if somebody just finds out they have breast cancer and they're going to take iodine for three

00:01:24,770 --> 00:01:29,810
months, you know, that's fine, especially if it tests fine for them.

00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:35,010
But if they're going to take iodine for a couple of years, the chance of them ended up developing

00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:44,530
Hashimoto's even prior to any hypothyroidism, primary hypothyroidism is very, very high.

00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:48,450
So that's why I'm not a fan of iodine.

00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:51,730
So I am a fan of iodine in acute situations.

00:01:51,730 --> 00:01:58,130
Let's say you have acute, you know, breast cancer or even acute radiation exposure

00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:02,530
can protect the thyroid for a very short period of time.

00:02:03,170 --> 00:02:05,490
But you have to be careful with iodine.

00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:09,570
You want to take a full-based iodine, a kelp-based iodine if you're going to take it

00:02:11,650 --> 00:02:14,690
and not long-term. That's just my opinion.

